From c255003dc74b305e6769cf3e8a10395324342b58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:07:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(pick): circle and arc centres as opt-in feature
 points

A picker that takes points can now opt in to the centre of a round
feature edge (PickKinds::centres). The centre is stored as the round
run it comes from and read back through #759's circle_of_run. It is
offered only while its edge is in sight; with Pick-through on it is
offered even when the edge is hidden. The three-points draft and an
axis by two points opt in. No other picker does. Those point slots, in
the GUI and over MCP (lay_part_on_points, set_part_axes), read a
circular edge chain as its centre. A straight or non-circular edge is
refused by name.

Refs #692

